title: Hold the Traditions? Part 2: Vain Traditions
description: Part 2 of a lesson on the Bible alone: examples written for our admonition, vain repetitions and the rosary, the second commandment removed, the altar of hewn stone, false prophets known by their fruits, proselytes twofold more the child of hell, and nothing shall separate us from the love of God.
output: lessons/heresies/hold-the-traditions-2-vain-traditions.html
context: yes

# Part 2 of 2. Built from the author's posts of 12-13 December 2022 (7076, 7077, 7082, 7083, 7084, 7085, 7086, 7087,
# 7096, 7099, 7104, 7105, 7106, 7107, 7108), which were filed with the Genesis 21 study and "spun out of a study on
# Genesis" (7108); in full and in their own order, but 7107 (posted after 7104) is set with the post it answers.
# Slide text is the author's own words; his history of the rosary and of the commandments is his, not checked here.
# Chapters the posts quote whole (1 Corinthians 10:6-15, Exodus 20, Matthew 7:15-29, Acts 7:48-53, Romans 8:31-39)
# are shown at the verses he speaks to, with a tap-to-read button; every verse is from the KJV.
# Fixed (in the deck and in the teaching's text in review/standalone.json): "visiting the inequalities of these
# heathens" -> "iniquities" (7083); "least the altar itself become an idol" -> "lest" (7085); "Eastern gnostic/Kabalah"
# -> "Kabbalah" (7099); verses typed in other words put back to the KJV: Exodus 20 ("the Lord" -> "the LORD", "of the
# that hate me" -> "of them that hate me"; 7083, 7085), Matthew 23:15 ("Woe to you, scribes and Pharissies.
# Hypocrites!" -> "Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites!"; 7107). Nothing else.

=== Introduction
--- Vain Traditions [title]
overline: Answering error • Hold the Traditions? Part 2 of 2
heading: Vain Traditions
sub: For our admonition • Vain repetitions • The second commandment • By their fruits • Nothing shall separate us
refs: Mark 7:13; Matthew 6:7; Exodus 20:4-5; Romans 8:38-39
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any reference to read the verse.

=== For our admonition
--- Written for Our Admonition
kicker: 1 Corinthians 10
scripture: 1 Corinthians 10:11-13 | mark: they are written for our admonition; God is faithful
center: [[1 Corinthians 10:6-15|Read 1 Corinthians 10:6–15]]

--- A Snare and a Stumbling Block
kicker: 1 Peter 1
p: The amazing thing about the Bible is how God, knowing the hearts of men, explains everything clearly, including correcting the mistaken understanding and false premises of heresy.
p: But when man rejects scripture, replacing the word of God with vain traditions and the logic of man, the truth of scripture becomes a snare and a stumbling block.
scripture: 1 Peter 1:18-21 | mark: received by tradition from your fathers

=== Vain repetitions
--- The Rosary
kicker: Matthew 6
p: The "Rosary" is a pagan blasphemy that requires vain, repetitive prayers. Ten times as many to a human, Mary, than to the purported "God" being prayed to.
p: The earliest reference to a rosary (boberkhas) is in their "Jain Canon" (456 AD) These boberkhas had various numbers of beads 6,9,12,18,36 (any sub-multiple of Kabbalah's 108). Islam (610 AD) uses a rosary of 99 beads, one for each of the names of God. Buddhists have 108 prayer beads on their string. The Rosary is of pagan origin and no Christian prior to 1000 AD used beads to pray.

--- Use Not Vain Repetitions
kicker: Matthew 6
p: Jesus forbids repetitive prayer in **Matthew 6:7-8**
scripture: Matthew 6:7-8 | mark: use not vain repetitions, as the heathen do
p: Another vain tradition of men that scripture explicitly commands against.

--- Enter into Thy Closet
kicker: Matthew 6 • Psalm 1
big: Matthew 6:6 | mark: pray to thy Father which is in secret
big: Psalm 1:2 | mark: in his law doth he meditate day and night
p: Remember, we are to delight in scripture and meditate on scripture night and day.
p: We are not to pray in vain repetitive prayers, using Eastern gnostic/Kabbalah prayer beads, kneeling and praying before idols.

--- Professing Themselves to Be Wise
kicker: Romans 1
scripture: Romans 1:21-23 | mark: Professing themselves to be wise, they became fools
center: [[Romans 1:18-25|Read Romans 1:18–25]]

=== The second commandment
--- Edited Commandments
kicker: Exodus 20
p: A Catholic "Pope" ordered the 2nd of the 10 commandments be edited, so they could use idols, statues & images in worship. They split the 10th commandment on coveting into two commandments so they could still have 10 in number.
p: Don't believe this? Look at the list of 10 commandments published by the Roman Catholic church! Their list of Commandments published to this day do not include the words from **Exodus 20:3-5**
scripture: Exodus 20:3-5 | mark: Thou shalt not make unto thee any graven image

--- Our God Is a Jealous God
kicker: Exodus 20
p: To worship idols or graven images of anyone or anything is to despise God and breaks His commandment, visiting the iniquities of these heathens on to their 3rd and 4th generation.
p: Our God is a jealous God. Amen!
p: Imagine rewriting the commandments given by God to justify wicked Idolatry? One could ask how it is they expect to follow the commandments of God to make themselves self-righteous, when they don't even know what they are, and their very practice is in defiance of God's word.

--- An Altar of Earth
kicker: Exodus 20
p: Here is the complete text of **Exodus 20**, note God reiterates His command against idols and even adds to it not to make an altar of cut stone, or crafted by hands lest the altar itself become an idol. Today, in Catholic churches, they genuflect before their hewn altars, worshiping their own works.
scripture: Exodus 20:23-25 | mark: thou shalt not build it of hewn stone
center: [[Exodus 20:1-26|Read Exodus 20]]

=== By their fruits
--- Upon a Rock
kicker: Matthew 7
p: Thank God for His word that we may build our faith upon the rock, unchanging and unmoving, while those perishing build their house upon the shifting sands of their own vain imagination and worthless tradition!
scripture: Matthew 7:24-25 | mark: which built his house upon a rock
center: [[Matthew 7:15-29|Read Matthew 7:15–29]]

--- Ye Shall Know Them by Their Fruits
kicker: Matthew 7
scripture: Matthew 7:15-18 | mark: Beware of false prophets; A good tree cannot bring forth evil fruit, neither can a corrupt tree bring forth good fruit
p: Remember, here Jesus warns against false prophets, and judging by their fruit, being proselytes. Those who adhere to their false doctrine.
p: Just as those who share the Gospel produce good fruit, those who bring another gospel are accursed, and their fruit, evil.

--- I Never Knew You
kicker: Matthew 7
p: And Jesus goes further, giving us a glimpse of those bad fruits, coming before Him in judgment in the very next verses:
scripture: Matthew 7:21-23 | mark: I never knew you: depart from me, ye that work iniquity
p: They rely on their works to save them, and Jesus says He never knew them. They are disobedient to the will of the Father.

--- The Father's Will
kicker: John 6
scripture: John 6:39-40 | mark: that every one which seeth the Son, and believeth on him, may have everlasting life
fig: Ephesians 5:6 | Ephesians 5:6
fig: 2 Thessalonians 1:8 | 2 Thessalonians 1:8

--- Twofold More the Child of Hell
kicker: Matthew 23 • Acts 7
big: Matthew 23:15 | mark: twofold more the child of hell than yourselves
p: This applies to false churches, accursed, who went out throughout the world to conquer for political gain and wealth, but damned millions with their false gospel.
scripture: Acts 7:48-50 | mark: the most High dwelleth not in temples made with hands
center: [[Acts 7:48-53|Read Acts 7:48–53]]

=== Nothing shall separate us
--- If God Be for Us
kicker: Romans 8
scripture: Romans 8:31-34 | mark: If God be for us, who can be against us?; It is God that justifieth

--- The Love of God
kicker: Romans 8
scripture: Romans 8:38-39 | mark: shall be able to separate us from the love of God, which is in Christ Jesus our Lord
p: Amen.
p: That's eternal security BTW. Anyone saying that salvation is a "process" or can be lost is teaching another gospel and is accursed.
center: [[Romans 8:31-39|Read Romans 8:31–39]]

--- Liberty in Christ
center: All this spun out of a study on Genesis, and the understanding that we are at Liberty in Christ. But some seek to keep people in bondage to the law for salvation. Sad.
